# Ink deploy canary. Claude rewrites this file after a substantial change; InkWatch (scripts\ink-watch.ps1)
# notices the new modification time and runs scripts\ink-push.ps1: commit + push, Firestore rules, Worker.
# subject: becomes the commit subject; everything after body: becomes the commit body.
last_tick: 2026-09-18T12:05:00Z
subject: Toolbar: Heading/Quote/Divider/List/Button/Image/Keep-me no longer eat the selection
body:
- Root cause: those buttons used a fixed template (e.g. "> Quoted line") and inserted it over whatever range was selected, silently discarding the selected text instead of using it.
- Quote and List now fold every line of the selection into "> "/"- " lines (falling back to placeholder lines only when nothing is selected), so a whole passage becomes a quote or list without losing a word.
- Heading, Button, Image and the Keep-me button now use the selection as their title/label/alt-text when there is one, instead of ignoring it.
- Divider has no text slot to absorb a selection into, so it no longer touches the selection at all -- it inserts itself right after the selection, leaving the selected text exactly as it was.
- Verified all of the above (with and without a selection, single- and multi-line) against the shared renderer before shipping.
